# EVERY fixture here must be ENUMERATED on the out-of-profile path, never
# silently dropped and never merely counted -- a dropped axiom is an incoherence
# the reasoner subsequently cannot see. Each yields non-empty coverage.omitted,
# so the verdict is INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2), never coherent.
# #
# Datatype properties, data ranges, literals in logical position --
# concrete domains are out of scope; the consumer partitions them and keeps a
# told-coherence side-check rather than HOWL growing a concrete domain.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix swrl: <http://www.w3.org/2003/11/swrl#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :d a owl:DatatypeProperty .
:d rdfs:domain :A ; rdfs:range xsd:integer .
:A rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :d ;
                     owl:someValuesFrom xsd:integer ] .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual ; :d 42 .
